                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support><p>A rectangular cippus/stele of the local limestone, finished smooth on all sides. Intact left and part of front and base and lower right, but damaged across the upper right. The top is preserved at the upper left, but the top of the face is lost, and theoretically there is space for a first line of text, if it were inscribed right up to the top of the front face (unlikely).</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone" type="stone.limestone" subtype="unverified" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html">limestone</material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.stele" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/250">stele</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">64</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">37.5</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">29.5</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.damaged"/>
		    </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout><p>Two visible lines of Greek letters, decreasing in size, across the upper part of the front face. Line 1 more widely spaced than line 2 and slightly inset.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.chiselled" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">chiselled</rs>
                                	<damage ana="#text_condition.incomplete"/>
			</layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>Elegant thinly carved letters. The trace of sigma on line 1 suggests a rather open four-bar sigma; Epsilon has short middle bar; Pi has short right hand hasta; omicron is sligthly smaller than other letters; Mu has vertical outer strokes, half-length inner strokes.</p>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line1">Line 1</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="42" atMost="50">42-50</height>
                                </dimensions>
                                <locus from="line2" to="line2">Line 2</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="30" atMost="42">30-42</height>
                                </dimensions>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line2">Interlineation line 1 to 2</locus>
                                <dimensions type="interlinear">
                                    <height unit="mm"/>
                                </dimensions>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
